    "q-1110": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1110",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-5{log}_{5}⁡(y)$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "The laws of logarithms are:\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)+{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(ab)$ - the product rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡(a)-{log}_{n}⁡(b)={log}_{n}⁡(\\frac{a}{b})$ - the quotient rule\n\n- ${log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)$ - the power rule\n\nUsing the power rule and then the quotient rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-5{log}_{5}⁡(y) & ={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{1/2})-{log}_{5}⁡({y}^{5}) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(\\sqrt{x})-{log}_{5}⁡({y}^{5}) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{y}^{5}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-1110-a",
